      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s early water power came from the Stratton and Pymatuning creeks, fueling mills that helped shape its early industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.kinsmantownship.org/about",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A covered bridge once spanned the Pymatuning, but an ice jam destroyed it, a reminder of the creek’s power.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.kinsmantownship.org/about",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Kinsman Public Library’s Historical Room houses books and artifacts related to famed lawyer Clarence Darrow, a native of the township.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.kinsmantownship.org/about",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Peter Allen Inn, once the town doctor’s home, now serves as a historic eatery in the former town hall.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.kinsmantownship.org/about",
